{"title":"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#=_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">= Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Explanation_of_the_last_step\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Explanation of the last step</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#An_alternate_last_step\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">An alternate last step</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The graphs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/c/98c7b0888bd4f62553212887fee4136bbdfa470b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = -|x-a| + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/1/3919aa9305e70a777b00ba4d5067bd85a278509e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = |x-c| + d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" /> intersect at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/9/ea9d3308a17610dcb38bfd84b443bdd0ea403605.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/f/91f8c8232fd46a61eca8423bbd3cec33adb70e74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(8,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/8/fb837dc059a93f257aed66ef84d279c516fca180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/f/19f5438c5c421a096736baae0aa3c2ad3a26d093.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } 7 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } 8 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } 10 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } 13\\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"369\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h1><span id=\".3D_Solution_1\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"=_Solution_1\">= Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: = Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<p>Each of the graphs consists of two orthogonal half-lines. In the first graph both point downwards at a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8adb649f063149ebc97d3ee58c4fd38d4c440846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> angle, in the second graph they point upwards. One can easily find out that the only way how to get these graphs to intersect in two points is the one depicted below:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/a/93aefed33c80d950ab05de405ba58ba40e8c6557.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.5cm); pair X=(2,5), Y=(8,3); draw ( (-1,2) -- (4,7) -- (10,1) ); draw ( (-1,8) -- (6,1) -- (10,5) ); label(&quot;$(2,5)$&quot;,X,W*1.5); label(&quot;$(8,3)$&quot;,Y,E*1.5); [/asy]\" width=\"268\" height=\"168\" /></center>\n<p>Obviously, the maximum of the first graph is achieved when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed47ef35959c171399e8f18eed4b517223823c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=a$\" width=\"44\" height=\"8\" />, and its value is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/b/8ab7944bcb9c8e56051920ce65b2dca3151b78f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-0+b=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />. Similarly, thminimum of the other graph is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/e/79e31171b9eaf222673b566ed3cf773e0f0b532c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(c,d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore the two remaining vertices of the area between the graphs are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/e/79e31171b9eaf222673b566ed3cf773e0f0b532c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(c,d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>As the area has four right angles, it is a rectangle. Without actually computing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> we can therefore conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93f6e68f677a3ab03e1e681ff765c4cac23dd64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+c=2+8=\\boxed{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"158\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Explanation_of_the_last_step\">Explanation of the last step</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Explanation of the last step\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>This is a property all rectangles in the coordinate plane have. \n</p><p>For a proof, note that for any rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> its center can be computed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/e/dee4ef909a3b802ea04fcdecf7b674cb85f73522.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A+C)/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" /> and at the same time as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/9/549f04fe01de2c7d0d301bbab9cab614ddc107aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(B+D)/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />. In our case, we can compute that the center is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/1/c0109a7402ed9d7bcb5818dddea14e7c1523d963.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{2+8}2,\\frac{5+3}2\\right)=(5,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"186\" height=\"43\" />, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259b163eebd67addfdf18b917640cb23a13e320c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a+c}2=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"76\" height=\"35\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e118051e873ef0fa29a2586209c351ef24aeca7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+c=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/a/dbabfa61852e5f3b12b67e713302a6fa63efefee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.5cm); pair X=(2,5), Y=(8,3); draw ( (-1,2) -- (4,7) -- (10,1) ); draw ( (-1,8) -- (6,1) -- (10,5) ); draw ( (4,7) -- (6,1) ); draw ( (2,5) -- (8,3) ); label(&quot;$(2,5)$&quot;,X,W*1.5); label(&quot;$(8,3)$&quot;,Y,E*1.5); label(&quot;$(a,b)$&quot;,(4,7),N); label(&quot;$(c,d)$&quot;,(6,1),S); [/asy]\" width=\"268\" height=\"202\" /></center>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"An_alternate_last_step\">An alternate last step</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: An alternate last step\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We can easily compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> using our picture. \n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/5520e18e1d8da50a9e38ae546ff57b35356af467.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.5cm); pair X=(2,5), Y=(8,3); draw ( (-1,2) -- (4,7) -- (10,1) ); draw ( (-1,8) -- (6,1) -- (10,5) ); label(&quot;$(2,5)$&quot;,X,W*1.5); label(&quot;$(8,3)$&quot;,Y,E*1.5); label(&quot;$(a,b)$&quot;,(4,7),N); label(&quot;$(c,d)$&quot;,(6,1),S); [/asy]\" width=\"268\" height=\"202\" /></center>\n<p>Consider the first graph on the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/2/1629783d7b0a005aa3c5aa870578de690b0d8e69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[2,8]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" />. The graph starts at height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then rises for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/c/61c1dd3bbde066f5334db006cebf1c06cbe03807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-2$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> steps to the height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/5/d4521511b24f8fe40715d0dc87b179ef573e3fac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=5+(a-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />, and then falls for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/f/e3fb352c7c663a8405c7f0043504b6eea0746f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8-a$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> steps to the height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/e/0fef4d34860a47e7e7355acc5e5ed42191d66d49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3=5+(a-2)-(8-a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"195\" height=\"18\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/f/c7ffa3b8792f0170bce1ab6008e907343100d70e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />. Similarly we compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/b/4eb76404ee79952dcc555464b061509299789b09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e118051e873ef0fa29a2586209c351ef24aeca7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+c=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Plug the coordinates into the two equations and set the equations equal to each other. The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> terms cancel out and you're left with just the following.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/e/dee3ac4c9d5695d684a85a78f9ddf6ce9a8b4a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|3-a| - |2-a| = |2-c| - |3-c|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"267\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>If we solve individually for the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> by setting both absolute values on the right to positive and setting one absolute value on the left to a negative, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f98b3f405113241659d8c8db2ea3480346db4d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />. Doing the same with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/d/7dd32a3f4397c1dc8606e89d5a85198d87fa27fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 6$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e118051e873ef0fa29a2586209c351ef24aeca7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+c=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME\" title=\"1999 AHSME\">1999 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1999 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1999\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems